seo-writer re-implements a static-HTML subset of those rules in Python (pure
standard library, no runtime dependency on the upstream TypeScript project).
The subset covers everything checkable from a single fetched document, its
response headers, and the robots.txt / sitemap.xml captured alongside it;
cross-page checks (JS rendering, Core Web Vitals, link graphs, hreflang
networks, redirect chains) are planned for a later phase.

Attribution also appears in the module docstring of
`src/seo_writer/seo_rules.py` and in the `rubric` metadata of every
`seo-audit.yaml` produced by `seo-writer onboard fetch`.
